t written Mongolian law.\n5. He sought to provide equal protection under the law for all citizens, regardless of their social status or wealth.\n6. Genghis Khan\'s principles are still valued in modern-day Mongolia as President Tsakhiagiin Elbegdorj has noted.\n7. The Ikh Zasag law included heavy punishments for corruption and bribery.\n8. The President sees Genghis Khan as a historical figure that could serve as an example for combating corruption today.\n9. Genghis Khan\'s focus on justice and equality reflects a timeless approach to governance.\n10. The legacy of Genghis Khan continues to shape Mongolia as a country, including its political and legal framework.\nTopic: Genghis Khan\nWhat innovation in Mongolian language is credited to Genghis Khan?\nAnswer:\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[151643], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=64, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [10061, 594, 4226, 264, 3405, 5961, 323, 3529, 285, 974, 624, 14582, 25, 9608, 25, 479, 826, 25235, 24287, 374, 26361, 438, 825, 315, 279, 20469, 6036, 304, 90750, 594, 3840, 13, 1260, 374, 8480, 369, 279, 48079, 315, 279, 43439, 3069, 438, 264, 4948, 323, 21551, 9569, 1576, 1052, 572, 902, 42690, 9569, 1948, 279, 38403, 429, 1030, 12752, 37623, 13, 1260, 48580, 1657, 43439, 337, 30906, 323, 3897, 19753, 323, 30326, 2337, 264, 882, 315, 4558, 94913, 38207, 1948, 38403, 13, 1260, 374, 1083, 2661, 6668, 369, 279, 16800, 315, 279, 8606, 43439, 88008, 5316, 323, 279, 9688, 315, 279, 358, 30664, 1863, 300, 351, 320, 21396, 16713, 701, 279, 1156, 5326, 43439, 88008, 2329, 13, 330, 40, 30664, 1863, 300, 351, 2329, 17827, 2337, 479, 826, 25235, 24287, 