INFO 07-17 13:06:34 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-de613563df0d4b7694925a70d0a7b49d-0: prompt: "Let's answer a question directly and concisely.\nQuestion: Context: This means that in a closed system of particles, there are no internal forces that are unbalanced. That is, the action-reaction force shared between any two objects in a closed system will not cause the center of mass of the system to accelerate. The constituent objects only accelerate with respect to each other, the system itself remains unaccelerated. Alternatively, if an external force acts on the system, then the center of mass will experience an acceleration proportional to the magnitude of the external force divided by the mass of the system.:19-1\nImplications: 1. In a closed system of particles, unbalanced internal forces between particles will cause the center of mass of the system to accelerate.\n2. The action-reaction force between any two objects in a closed system will not cause the center of mass of the system to accelerate.\n3. The center of mass of the system remains unaccelerated unless an external force acts on the system.\n4. If an external force acts on the system, the center of mass will experience an acceleration proportional to the magnitude of the external force divided by the mass of the system.\n5. The constituent objects in a closed system will only accelerate with respect to each other.\n6. A closed system of particles will have an unchanging center of mass, unless an external force acts on the system.\n7. The acceleration of the center of mass of a closed system will not be caused by internal forces, but rather by external forces.\n8. The center of mass of a closed system of particles will remain unchanged unless an external force acts on it.\n9. The center of mass of a closed system of particles can only be accelerated by an external force.\n10. The acceleration of the center of mass of a closed system of particles is directly proportional to the magnitude of the external force applied to the system.\nTopic: Force\nWhat experiences acceleration when external force is applied to a system?\nAnswer:\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[151643], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=64, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [10061, 594, 4226, 264, 3405, 5961, 323, 3529, 285, 974, 624, 14582, 25, 9608, 25, 1096, 3363, 429, 304, 264, 7877, 1849, 315, 18730, 11, 1052, 525, 902, 5306, 8437, 429, 525, 650, 58402, 13, 2938, 374, 11, 279, 1917, 5504, 1311, 5344, 6094, 1948, 894, 1378, 6171, 304, 264, 7877, 1849, 686, 537, 5240, 279, 4126, 315, 3072, 315, 279, 1849, 311, 42780, 13, 576, 74064, 6171, 1172, 42780, 448, 5091, 311, 1817, 1008, 11, 279, 1849, 5086, 8458, 650, 43888, 261, 657, 13, 38478, 11, 421, 458, 9250, 5344, 14056, 389, 279, 1849, 11, 1221, 279, 4126, 315, 3072, 686, 3139, 458, 30803, 54172, 311, 279, 25621, 315, 279, 9250, 5344, 17779, 553, 279, 3072, 315, 279, 1849, 18469, 16, 24, 12, 16, 198, 25216, 10709, 25, 220, 16, 13, 758, 264, 7877, 1849, 315, 18730, 11, 650, 58402, 5306, 8437, 1948, 18730, 686, 5240, 279, 4126, 315, 3072, 315, 279, 1849, 311, 42780, 624, 17, 13, 576, 1917, 5504, 1311, 5344, 1948, 894, 1378, 6171, 304, 264, 7877, 1849, 686, 537, 5240, 279, 4126, 315, 3072, 315, 279, 1849, 311, 42780, 624, 18, 13, 576, 4126, 315, 3072, 315, 279, 1849, 8458, 650, 43888, 261, 657, 7241, 458, 9250, 5344, 14056, 389, 279, 1849, 624, 19, 13, 1416, 458, 9250, 5344, 14056, 389, 279, 1849, 11, 279, 4126, 315, 3072, 686, 3139, 458, 30803, 54172, 311, 279, 25621, 315, 279, 9250, 5344, 17779, 553, 279, 3072, 315, 279, 1849, 624, 20, 13, 576, 74064, 6171, 304, 264, 7877, 1849, 686, 1172, 