INFO 07-17 13:07:00 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-b37a7bb74ec840398d3a1b5f88a381ba-0: prompt: "Let's answer a question directly and concisely.\nQuestion: Context: In past times, corporal punishment (spanking or paddling or caning or strapping or birching the student in order to cause physical pain) was one of the most common forms of school discipline throughout much of the world. Most Western countries, and some others, have now banned it, but it remains lawful in the United States following a US Supreme Court decision in 1977 which held that paddling did not violate the US Constitution.\nImplications: 1. Corporal punishment, although once widely practiced, is no longer commonly used as a method of discipline in schools.\n2. In many countries, corporal punishment is not permitted in educational institutions.\n3. In Western countries, there is now an increasing trend towards the ban of corporal punishment.\n4. The United States remains an exception to the global trend against corporal punishment in schools, as the case of the US Supreme Court decision in 1977 sets it apart.\n5. The US Supreme Court decision in 1977 upholding the legality of paddling in schools in the United States set a precedent that has yet to be overturned.\n6. Countries that continue to allow corporal punishment in schools may be seen as holding onto archaic practices that do not reflect the current global consensus on the matter.\nTopic: Teacher\nHow common was the form of corporal punishment in the past?\nAnswer:\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[151643], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=64, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [10061,