INFO 07-17 13:10:05 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-bf51ce7bce094f50b180d0b5d0c8d3b1-0: prompt: 'Let\'s answer a question directly and concisely.\nQuestion: Context: "The Islamic State", formerly known as the "Islamic State of Iraq and the Levant" and before that as the "Islamic State of Iraq", (and called the acronym Daesh by its many detractors), is a Wahhabi/Salafi jihadist extremist militant group which is led by and mainly composed of Sunni Arabs from Iraq and Syria. In 2014, the group proclaimed itself a caliphate, with religious, political and military authority over all Muslims worldwide. As of March 2015[update], it had control over territory occupied by ten million people in Iraq and Syria, and has nominal control over small areas of Libya, Nigeria and Afghanistan. (While a self-described state, it lacks international recognition.) The group also operates or has affiliates in other parts of the world, including North Africa and South Asia.\nImplications: 1. The Islamic State is a Wahhabi/Salafi jihadist extremist group composed primarily of Sunni Arabs from Iraq and Syria.\n2. The group has been known by different names, including "Islamic State of Iraq and the Levant" and "Islamic State of Iraq".\n3. In 2014, the group claimed the establishment of a caliphate, asserting religious, political, and military authority over all Muslims worldwide.\n4. As of March 2015, the Islamic State had control over territory occupied by ten million people in Iraq and Syria, and had nominal control over small areas of Libya, Nigeria, and Afghanistan.\n5. The group\'s territory lacks international recognition as it is not recognized as a state.\n6. The group operates or has affiliates in other parts of the world, including North Africa and South Asia.\n7. The group\'s activities and claims have generated significant controversy and opposition, as it is perceived as a threat to stability and security in the regions it operates in, as well as to the broader global community.\n8. The Islamic State\'s Wahhabi/Salafi ideology is considered extremist and violent by many, and its goals are seen as at odds with the values of liberal democracies and international law.\n9. The group\'s control over territory and resources has led to concerns about its ability to finance its operations, including its access to oil revenue.\n10. The group\'s use of violent tactics, including the targeting of civilians, has resulted in widespread condemnation and calls for international intervention to combat its influence and prevent further violence.\nTopic: Islamism\nWhat type of group is The Islamic State?\nAnswer:\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[151643], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=64, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [10061, 594, 4226, 264, 3405, 5961, 323, 3529, 285, 974, 624, 14582, 25, 9608, 25, 330, 785, 15203, 3234, 497, 33733, 3881, 438, 279, 330, 97173, 3234, 315, 11093, 323, 279, 27022, 517, 1, 323, 1573, 429, 438, 279, 330, 97173, 3234, 315, 11093, 497, 320, 437, 2598, 279, 74514, 14235, 4288, 553, 1181, 1657, 34353, 21161, 701, 374, 264, 69590, 61595, 11374, 278, 45910, 96044, 55782, 51282, 1874, 892, 374, 6069, 553, 323, 14576, 23415, 315, 55010, 57609, 504, 11093, 323, 12623, 13, 758, 220, 17, 15, 16, 19, 11, 279, 1874, 61911, 5086, 264, 1620, 15261, 349, 11, 448, 10381, 11, 4948, 323, 6277, 11198, 916, 678, 19503, 15245, 13, 1634, 315, 5470, 220, 17, 15, 16, 20, 58, 2386, 1125, 432, 1030, 2524, 916, 17971, 24367, 553, 5779, 3526, 1251, 304, 11093, 323, 12623, 11, 323, 702, 46755, 2524, 916, 2613, 5671, 315, 36959, 11, 28158, 323, 20500, 13, 320, 7983, 264, 656, 50604, 1584, 11, 4