INFO 07-17 13:21:31 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-b1072e30d8fe4b6693bbc6f819bb523f-0: prompt: 'Let\'s answer a question directly and concisely.\nQuestion: Context: As a result, by 1206 Temüjin had managed to unite or subdue the Merkits, Naimans, Mongols, Keraites, Tatars, Uyghurs, and other disparate smaller tribes under his rule. It was a monumental feat for the "Mongols" (as they became known collectively). At a Khuruldai, a council of Mongol chiefs, Temüjin was acknowledged as "Khan" of the consolidated tribes and took the new title "Genghis Khan". The title Khagan was not conferred on Genghis until after his death, when his son and successor, Ögedei, took the title for himself and extended it posthumously to his father (as he was also to be posthumously declared the founder of the Yuan dynasty). This unification of all confederations by Genghis Khan established peace between previously warring tribes and a single political and military force under Genghis Khan.\nImplications: 1. Genghis Khan unified various tribes and established a cohesive military force.\n2. The unification led to peace and cooperation among previously warring tribes.\n3. Genghis Khan was officially recognized as the "Khan" of the consolidated tribes.\n4. Genghis Khan\'s achievements laid the foundation for his posthumous designation as the founder of the Yuan dynasty and the builder of the Mongol Empire.\n5. Genghis Khan\'s unification of the tribes created a single political and military force under his leadership, which contributed to the establishment of the Mongol Empire.\nTopic: Genghis Khan\nBy what year had Temüjin created a significant "Mongol" tribal alliance?\nAnswer:\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[151643], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=64, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_lo