INFO 07-17 13:25:38 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-6f1f0deae70640e4a9b185afec16041d-0: prompt: "Let's answer a question directly and concisely.\nQuestion: Context: Although Kenya is the biggest and most advanced economy in east and central Africa, and has an affluent urban minority, it has a Human Development Index (HDI) of 0.519, ranked 145 out of 186 in the world. As of 2005, 17.7% of Kenyans lived on less than $1.25 a day. The important agricultural sector is one of the least developed and largely inefficient, employing 75% of the workforce compared to less than 3% in the food secure developed countries. Kenya is usually classified as a frontier market or occasionally an emerging market, but it is not one of the least developed countries.\nImplications: 1. Kenya's economy is the largest and most advanced in its region.\n2. It has an affluent urban minority.\n3. It has a relatively low Human Development Index (HDI) of 0.519, ranking 145 out of 186 countries.\n4. Around 17.7% of Kenyans live on less than $1.25 a day, indicating a significant portion of the population lives in poverty.\n5. The agricultural sector, which is crucial to Kenya's economy, is underdeveloped and inefficient.\n6. The sector employs 75% of the workforce, which is far higher than the percentage employed in the sector in food secure developed countries.\n7. The efficiency of the agricultural sector contributes to Kenya being classified as a frontier market or an emerging market.\n8. Kenya is not a Least Developed Country (LDC).\nTopic: Kenya\nWhat is Kenya's HDI?\nAnswer:\n", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[151643], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=64, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided