INFO 07-17 13:36:45 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-2ec7b8b3cc7b4300ab2f90ade238b43d-0: prompt: 'Let\'s answer a question directly and concisely.\nQuestion: Context: In 1952, following pressure from Tesla\'s nephew, Sava Kosanović, Tesla\'s entire estate was shipped to Belgrade in 80 trunks marked N.T. In 1957, Kosanović\'s secretary Charlotte Muzar transported Tesla\'s ashes from the United States to Belgrade. The ashes are displayed in a gold-plated sphere on a marble pedestal in the Nikola Tesla Museum.\nImplications: 1. Nikola Tesla had a significant amount of belongings, suggesting he may have been wealthy or well-known.\n2. His nephew, Sava Kosanović, felt compelled to protect Tesla\'s estate, indicating that it had value or significance.\n3. Kosanović\'s actions suggest that Tesla\'s work and/or personality may have been influential.\n4. The extensive shipping and display of Tesla\'s ashes in Belgrade indicate a high regard for his legacy or contribution to society.\n5. Tesla\'s ashes being displayed alongside a "marble pedestal" suggests that he is viewed as a legendary figure or highly respected individual.\n6. The transfer of Tesla\'s estate occurred a few years after his death in 1952, indicating that he was still respected in his lifetime.\n7. The ashes being "gold-plated" implies that Tesla was perceived as a valuable or extraordinary individual.\n8. The fact that his nephew made efforts to preserve Tesla\'s estate and legacy highlights the importance that his family placed on his work and influence.\n9. The museum in Belgrade displaying Tesla\'s ashes suggests that he has inspired other people and generations to appreciate his work.\n10. The transfer and exhibition of Tesla\'s estate and ashes occurred in 1952, 1957, and possibly later, which shows that there was at least some level of interest in honoring his legacy.\n\nLet\'s read the following passage and produce a list of implications derived directly or indirectly from the content.\n\nPassage:\nNikola Tesla (Serbian Cyrillic: Никола Тесла;[a] July 10, 1856July 7, 1943) was a Serbian-American inventor, electrical engineer, mechanical engineer, and physicist. He is best known for his contributions to the design of the modern alternating current (AC) electricity supply system.\n\nImplications:\n1. Nikola Tesla was a prominent inventor and scientist with multiple fields of expertise.\n2. He was born in July 1856 and died in July 1943.\n3. Tesla was Serbian by origin, and later became American.\n4. He is primarily recognized for his role in the development of the modern AC electric power system.\n5. Tesla was influential in the field of electrical engineering and electrical engineering specifically.\n6. His inventions and innovations contributed to the advancement of science and technology in the late 19th and early 20th centuries.\n7. AC electric power systems are a fundamental aspect of modern society and Tesla played a significant role in their development.\n8. Tesla\'s work in electrical and mechanical engineering, as well as physics, indicates that he was a highly knowledgeable and experienced individual.\n9. His work has had a lasting impact on the fields of electrical engineering and power systems.\n10. Tesla\'s accomplishments have earned him a place among the most important inventors and scientists in history.\nTopic: Nikola Tesla\nWhere was Tesla\'s property sent?\nAnswer:\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[151643], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=64, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [10061, 594, 4226, 264, 3405, 5961, 323, 3529, 285, 974, 624, 14582, 25, 9608, 25, 758, 220, 16, 24, 20, 17, 11