INFO 07-17 13:42:03 [logger.py:43] Received request cmpl-c57d8cc030df4bce8282670095ed93b4-3: prompt: 'Let\'s answer a question directly and concisely.\nQuestion: Context: In 2013, the Peabody Awards honoured Doctor Who with an Institutional Peabody "for evolving with technology and the times like nothing else in the known television universe." The programme is listed in Guinness World Records as the longest-running science fiction television show in the world, the "most successful" science fiction series of all time—based on its over-all broadcast ratings, DVD and book sales, and iTunes traffic— and for the largest ever simulcast of a TV drama with its 50th anniversary special. During its original run, it was recognised for its imaginative stories, creative low-budget special effects, and pioneering use of electronic music (originally produced by the BBC Radiophonic Workshop).\nImplications: 1. Doctor Who has successfully adapted to technological advancements and modern times.\n2. The show is a long-running science fiction series with a global audience.\n3. It is the most successful science fiction series in terms of broadcast ratings, DVD and book sales, and iTunes traffic.\n4. It holds the Guinness World Record for the longest-running science fiction television show.\n5. Doctor Who has a large following and a significant impact on popular culture.\n6. The show has been recognized for its imaginative stories and creative use of special effects.\n7. The programme has pioneered the use of electronic music.\n8. Doctor Who has been impactful through its 50th anniversary special.\n\nLet\'s read the following passage and produce a list of implications derived directly or indirectly from the content.\n\nPassage:\nAmerican Horror Story: Asylum\n\nIn the first season, 2010, Julia was introduced. The filming location was Checkered Past Studios, Burbank, California. Julia’s character Julia Harris was played by Denise O’Herlihy. Her character’s "elaborately cut hair was intended as an homage to the most famous patient held at the institution, Grace Murray." The rest of the costumes were styled by at Tiffany Tew. Julia’s costume was specifically fashioned from "25 layers of tulle" which took 17 hours to be fashioned. The show’s uniforms and wardresses were made by Edith Rohm, "Carter Biebl set design for the patient’s world was intentionally out of date." The property Biebl chose to decorate "was what’s left of the old oil mills in Elysian Park" the landscaping for that, he said, came from Janet Huff, the set decorator.\n\nImplications:\n1. The first season of American Horror Story: Asylum premiered in 2010.\n2. Checkered Past Studios in Burbank, California served as the filming location.\n3. The character Julia Harris was played by Denise O\'Herlihy.\n4. The character\'s elaborately cut hair was inspired by Grace Murray, a notable patient of the institution.\n5. Tiffany Tew was responsible for the styling of Julia\'s costume, which consisted of 25 layers of tulle.\n6. It took 17 hours to fashion Julia\'s costume.\n7. The show\'s uniforms and wardresses were designed by Edith Rohm.\n8. Carter Biebl was responsible for designing the patient\'s world, which was intentionally out of date.\n9. The property Biebl chose to decorate was what remained of the old oil mills in Elysian Park.\n10. Janet Huff was responsible for the landscaping of the property.\nTopic: Doctor Who\nWhat year did Doctor Who win a Peabody award?\nAnswer:\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=0, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[151643], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=64, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None, extra_args=None), prompt_token_ids: [10061, 594, 4226, 264, 3405, 5961, 323, 3529, 285,